bring class/order/complement.tung
bring is.tung
bring type/powerset.tung
bring type/two.tung
bring type/zero.tung

## `f diagonal g` taketh each `a` to `g` of `a`'s own value `a (a f)`.
show let diagonal: [@α: *, @β: *, f: [α, α, β], g: [β, β], α, β] ≔ {
  a ^ (a (a f)) g
}

## lawvere's fixed point theorem: when some `a f` is `f diagonal g`, the value
## `a (a f)` is a fixed point of `g`. so if `f` reacheth every function
## `[α, β]`, every `g: [β, β]` hath a fixed point.
show let lawvere
  : [@α: *, @β: *, f: [α, α, β], g: [β, β], a: α, hit: (a f) = (f diagonal g),
    ((a (a f)) g) = (a (a f))]
  ≔ ({h ^ a h} leibnitz hit) symmetry

## no truth value is its own complement.
let lemma_∁_fixed: [b: 𝟚, (b ∁) ≠ b] ≔ match b {
  yea;
  nay ^ {}
}

## cantor's theorem: no `a f` is the subset of the values outside their own
## subset, so no `f` reacheth every subset of `α`.
show let cantor: [@α: *, f: [α, α powerset], a: α, (a f) ≠ (f diagonal ∁)] ≔ {
  hit ^ (a (a f)) lemma_∁_fixed (f lawvere ∁ a hit)
}
